{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nParis, in the evening. Yesterday I visited Versailles. The main building is still empty, which gives off a certain desolation, but the Trianons are furnished. They have laid out the garden there in so-called English style: artificial rocks, Swiss huts – a kind of arbitrary arrangement that seeks to outdo the natural order. In the orangery stands a tree that was planted in 1420; its age is a silent admonition, while the 130 marble statues in the park remain merely stones.\n\nIt is strange how here history and the present touch each other without connecting. I saw no fountains, which troubled me little; water is not necessary to recognize the essence of things, even though it sharpens the sense of the eternal. My heart is with you in Berlin. The journey is arduous, but the thoughts are sharp.\n\nYour faithful Wilhelm"}}],"created":1795221218,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":188,"prompt_tokens":287,"total_tokens":475,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-XcYOPLmFvnEzrdIoDsTmJaPlrLP28YqP","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":287,"prompt_ms":430.164,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.498829268292683,"prompt_per_second":667.1873982946039,"predicted_n":188,"predicted_ms":4399.558,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.527048128342248,"predicted_per_second":42.50426974709732}}